course: dictionary
lesson: 4101
title: Learning about a giraffe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A giraffe is a very tall African animal with a very long neck, long legs and a coat with brown patches. You can build a picture of it from the words in the dictionary. Good readers do this with every new word.
explain: «Picture an animal so tall that a giraffe could almost walk under its belly.» The sentence uses the giraffe as a measure. If a giraffe could almost walk under the belly of that animal, the animal must be taller than a giraffe. So the giraffe is one of the tallest animals you can think of.
explain: «It wraps the tongue round acacia leaves to pull them from between the thorns.» Thorns are sharp, so the giraffe needs a long, strong tongue to reach leaves that other animals cannot reach. Context clues like these help you understand what a word means and what it does.
fact: A giraffe is a very tall African animal with a very long neck, long legs and a coat with brown patches.
fact: The giraffe is the tallest animal on land.
fact: A baby giraffe is called a calf.
fact: A group of giraffes can be called a herd or a tower.
fact: A giraffe's tongue is about 45 to 50 cm long and dark blue-black, which may protect it from sunburn, though scientists are not certain.
exercise: «Werribee and Monarto are huge open-range zoos where herds of giraffes roam.» What is a herd? | A type of long tongue | *A group of animals that move together | A zoo keeper | A single tall tree
exercise: What is a baby giraffe called? | A foal | A kid | *A calf | A cub
exercise: «The okapi lives only in the Congo forest and is the giraffe's closest living relative.» Which animal is the giraffe's closest living relative? | The rhino | The zebra | *The okapi | The lion
test: According to the lesson, why is a giraffe's long neck useful? | It helps it swim fast across rivers | *It helps it reach leaves high in trees | It helps it run quietly | It keeps it warm in winter
test: «A giraffe's tongue is about 45 to 50 cm long and dark blue-black.» What does the word long tell you about the tongue? | It is a tongue that can only be seen at night | It is a tongue that is sore and tired | It is a short tongue that looks small | *It is a long tongue, many centimetres from end to end
exam: Which meaning fits the word giraffe best? | *A very tall African animal with a long neck and brown patches | A thorny tree that grows in deserts | A bird from Australia that cannot fly | A small striped horse that lives in the sea
